WEBVTT

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:54.220
The crimson liquid trails down my goosey skin

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:54.220
Awadatsu Hada wo Tsutai Ochiru CRIMSON

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:58.410
Why do you wish for another punishment?

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:58.410
Why do you want Atarashii Batsu wo

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:03.160
These sweet scents floating with "blood"

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:03.160
Tadayou Amai Kaori wo Tada

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:07.720
Let the fragrances idle and drift about freely as I hoped they would

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:07.720
Asobasete Itai Dake Nano sa

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:15.400
Now please, hurry and pierce through me!

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:15.400
Dareka Boku wo Hayaku Uchinuite yo

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:20.550
Shoot me and put visible holes through my body

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:20.550
Shoot me Kantsuushita Juusou Ana ga Aku Hodo

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:25.020
Squeeze the thorny pistol grip,

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:25.020
Toge Darake no GRIP Nigiritsubuse

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:30.790
load the bullets that resemble red rosebuds,

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:30.790
Osanai Mada Tsubomi no You na Dangan de

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.900
and let me shoot through the flower!

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.900
Let me shoot through the flower!

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.340
Smear this world in rose!

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.340
Bara-iro ni Somare

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:02.400
You're— Keisuke?!

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.430
A-Akira?!

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:14.750
What're <i>you</i>  doing here?

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:18.380
I thought you might be here.

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:19.980
That's not what I'm meant.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.930
I was just so worried about you...

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.220
So you followed me?

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:29.160
Yeah.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:34.670
I'm glad you're safe at least.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.610
I did run into some trouble.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:38.940
But I ran and managed to escape.

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.310
You shouldn't be here.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:49.890
But I thought if there was any way I could help...

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:52.180
This isn't a game.

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:53.950
I don't need your help.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.200
I'm not leaving!

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:01.790
I don't even know how to get back.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:11.250
I won't go back.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:15.190
Fine.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:16.890
Ok.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:23.710
Thanks, Akira.

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:56.130
Akira?

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:57.570
I'm heading out.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:00.820
Where are you going?

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.460
Igra, of course.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.740
I've got some tags, after all.

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:10.950
If you lose, you may end up dying, huh?

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:12.240
Didn't I tell you already?

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:14.400
This isn't some kind of trivial game.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.760
I have to kill others too.

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:20.230
"Kill or be killed."

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.750
That's the rule here.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:25.700
Unless I defeat the top, Il Re,

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.510
I won't be able to get out of here.

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:31.090
I'll come too!

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.140
No way. Aren't you unarmed?

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:35.990
I don't want to wait for you all by myself!

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:41.390
Hold onto this.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:44.300
What about you, Akira?

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.300
Do you have a spare knife?

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:47.550
No, I don't.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.310
But then, what will you—

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:50.500
Keisuke!

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:51.780
Promise me now!

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:54.720
That you'll do everything you can to protect your own life!

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:57.750
Alright.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:58.710
I get it.

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:04.360
Wait up, Akira!

00:07:27.390 --> 00:07:29.390
Akira, over there...

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:38.830
Damn it!

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:43.440
Let's go.

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:45.420
Ah, okay.

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:49.300
And that's that!

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:54.510
I'll let you off the hook today.

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:13.620
Hold up!

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:20.700
Ah, you're that girl from before!

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:23.500
Sucks to be you!

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:24.840
I've got a you-know-what.

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:25.900
Wha—?!

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:27.790
Y-You have a—?!

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:34.450
Well, that's a minor detail.

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:37.290
This is my turf.

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:39.900
I have a problem with you guys weaseling your way in here.

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:41.500
Your turf?

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:42.410
That's right!

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:47.390
If you step into someone else's
territory, you have to pay an entry fee.

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:50.320
Entry fee? What the...

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:57.610
I take it that you two are going to participate in Igra, right?

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:04.640
Well, whatever then!

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:06.500
I've already found a reasonable spot to photograph

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:11.660
and you two are pretty good looking so I'll lift the entry fee this time around.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:13.970
Anyway, do you guys have any questions?

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:17.450
Do you know where we can get some weapons?

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.990
Weapons, huh?

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:21.490
How 'bout this?

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:26.350
Even a beginner could use this, you know.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:28.790
Then what'll you use?

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.240
I'm just lending it to you for now.

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:32.420
You can pay me back later.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:34.080
With your body.

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:36.150
What'd you say?!

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:37.520
Aren't you a guy?

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:43.290
Aw, come on! It was just a joke!

00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:45.990
I'm Rin!

00:09:45.990 --> 00:09:46.960
What about you guys?

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:50.050
I'm Akira.

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:51.300
He's Keisuke.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:53.780
Akira and Keisuke, huh?

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:58.450
So, Keisuke, are you really not going to participate in Igra?

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:00.760
This guy's—

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:01.840
In this town,

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:04.190
it's not unusual for folks to just die, you know.

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:07.100
Regardless of the fact that you're going to join in Igra or not, people do die.

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:09.740
That's why you should go and enjoy yourself!

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:14.820
Why don't you go listen to
someone explain how Igra works?

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:17.020
Okay...

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:19.640
All right! Let's go!

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:20.990
Where to?

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:22.710
We'll be going to the Castle.

00:10:22.710 --> 00:10:23.860
That's Arbitro's pad.

00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:25.280
Who's this Arbitro gu—

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:27.060
Come on, hurry hurry!

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.210
What are you so nervous about?

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.040
Alrighty.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:42.750
We're in front of the headquarters of the devilish drug organization, Vischio!

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:44.970
It's nicknamed the Castle!

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:47.500
It's pretty big.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:48.890
Totally!

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:54.180
From what I've heard, it served as some
kind of an event hall before the great war.

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:58.010
For drama plays and concerts and other stuff like that.

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:05.030
Then, after the great war, it just seemed
appropriate for Vischio members to occupy the area.

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:08.180
The inside of the Castle is full of chaos now. Pure chaos.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:09.240
Chaos?

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:10.730
You'll see what I mean once we get there.

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:16.120
Good job!

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:17.910
What brings you here?

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:20.140
The desire to participate in Igra.

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:23.340
Aren't you already participating?

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:25.340
I didn't say it was my desire.

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:26.620
Look behind me.

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:28.980
The big guy in blue overalls.

00:11:30.050 --> 00:11:31.940
Thanks for your help.

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:33.620
Very well.

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:34.430
Come in.

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:05.130
Seems like every time I come here, this place is full of strange shit.

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:07.560
So this is what that Arbitro guy likes?

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:08.890
Yup.

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:16.330
Who wishes to join Igra?

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:19.490
That would be me...

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:22.670
You must put this on first.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:31.470
This way.

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:34.970
Well, I'll be back after I go see what he says.

00:12:54.070 --> 00:12:55.110
Are you worried?

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:56.600
Not really.

00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:57.900
You're so lying!

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:02.600
You're against Keisuke participating in Igra. It's written all over your face!

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:06.840
That's for him to decide.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:11.180
Keisuke!

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:13.470
Welcome back!

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:15.580
Wait, where're your tags?

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:20.460
Did you give up on joining?

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:23.590
Yeah, about that...

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:24.650
I'm sorry.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:27.450
There's no need to apologize, you know.

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:28.560
Let's get back.

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:31.440
I thought this would happen!

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:34.850
You're so timid. I didn't think you could do it!

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:49.340
So guys! I'm going to meet up with a friend of mine.

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:50.200
You wanna tag along?

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:51.650
Friend?

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:52.810
Yup!

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:55.350
He asked me for a favor.

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:57.570
He's quite a well-rounded, knowledgeable old man.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:58.500
Lemme introduce him to you two.

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:01.630
I don't think there's a downside to meeting new people.

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:07.650
Erm...

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:10.350
Why are you being so nice to us, anyway?

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:15.510
Well, I've been in Igra for quite a while now.

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:17.350
I've decided to change up my
plans a bit since it's kinda boring.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:19.880
I'm tired of it.

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:21.940
Well aren't you laid-back?

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:24.320
Right on! But that's just since I'm strong already.

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:28.770
If I really wanted tags, I could just
pick on some lowbies and get them.

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:31.450
I never really did feel like targeting either of you.

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:34.960
Well, it's beneficial if you both
learn more about this place, no?

00:14:37.150 --> 00:14:38.290
Alright.

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:40.310
It's this way.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:55.890
Bah, it's the Executioners?

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.360
Executioners?

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:07.400
Well, just watch and you'll understand.

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:14.050
I said there's no point in trying to run away.

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:18.330
That's it! Too bad!

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:20.080
It's game over!

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:24.800
Hey, wasn't that cool?

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:26.790
That blonde guy is Gunji.

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:33.930
Damn, Mitsuko. You sure can fly.

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:38.730
The one with black hair is Kiriwar.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:41.660
You'll want to be wary of those guys.

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:43.900
They're moody and irresponsible.

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:47.600
They've made up false accusations and killed people before.

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:50.520
That would be?

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:52.000
That's Arbitro's dog.

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:53.350
D-Dog?

00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:56.870
Huh? What's that?

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:02.460
He says it was fair since he had all of those tags!

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:12.760
Does that guy have something on him?

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:18.200
For some reason, Fido here seems to be reacting to you.

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:21.810
You do have a scent.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:26.520
Sheesh, you playboy!

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:28.730
Seriously, what have you been doing?!

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:30.670
I told you that we should hurry and go already!

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:31.900
Come now, jeez.

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:35.000
We'll be in trouble if we upset these kind Executioners!

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:37.890
If we don't hurry, we'll just end up being hindrances to them!

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:41.100
So anyway, we're really, really sorry!

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:42.570
Annoying.

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:43.670
Yeah.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:49.300
Well, whatever.

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:52.690
We better get Fido back or else 'bitro gonna snap.

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:53.890
It's dinner time.

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:54.460
Yeah.

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:56.260
That was dangerous, huh?

00:16:56.670 --> 00:16:58.840
I was really worried about what might've happened.

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:01.440
Let's get there soon.

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:05.260
Our destination is practically right in front of our eyes.

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:23.670
Ah, there he is!

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:25.630
Gramps!

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:27.840
Yo, you're later than I expected.

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:30.920
Nah, we just got caught up with the Executioners.

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:32.650
There were two victims.

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:33.930
Were they criminals?

00:17:33.930 --> 00:17:35.370
Who knows.

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:36.800
Falsely accused, I wonder.

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:41.560
Well, who knows if losing two
people was a good thing or bad thing.

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:43.230
Anyway, where's the thing I asked for?

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:45.350
I brought it.

00:17:45.820 --> 00:17:46.600
Here!

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:49.500
All right, this is it!

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:51.770
Hm? Who're they? Your friends?

00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:53.660
Introduce them already!

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:55.820
I was gonna do that!

00:17:56.490 --> 00:17:58.860
Well, this one's Akira,

00:18:00.450 --> 00:18:02.280
and this would be Keisuke!

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:03.370
Hello.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:06.740
This cold, old man is Motomi.

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:08.940
The 'cold' part is too much.

00:18:09.530 --> 00:18:12.530
But why are you guys following Rin around?

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:14.670
He never shuts up.

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:16.770
Are you saying I'm noisy?

00:18:16.770 --> 00:18:18.310
I just got here!

00:18:18.310 --> 00:18:21.060
I was kind and courteous enough to show them over here!

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:23.550
Most people would consider that obnoxious and noisy.

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:25.830
Didn't you tell me before not to say that to other people?

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:27.640
Don't you actually love heating the trouble, after all?

00:18:29.130 --> 00:18:30.130
That may be so.

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:31.570
What's that photo, anyway?

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:36.590
This, huh? It's going to be used for some work I do.

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:38.200
I requested this from Rin.

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:39.750
Work?

00:18:40.210 --> 00:18:42.600
It's an information shop.

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:44.620
If it's not suspicious, it wouldn't even exist, right?

00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:46.550
An information shop...

00:18:46.550 --> 00:18:49.350
Well, after I stock up with a variety of news and gossip,

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:52.090
I make exchanges and get myself food that way.

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:55.450
Ta-da!

00:18:55.450 --> 00:18:57.680
I can get a lot of news with this!

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:00.280
Okay, let's see here!

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:04.150
Come now, Akira, how about just one shot?

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:05.730
I don't like being photographed.

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:07.010
I get it.

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:10.370
You don't want to take a picture with that weird old dude, huh?

00:19:11.050 --> 00:19:12.060
Well!

00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:16.070
He never did say that, you know.

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:17.450
Right, Akira?

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:20.570
Let's just make this a memoir of our meeting!

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:21.460
Right?

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:22.630
Sure...

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:24.350
All right, here I go!

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:25.370
Say cheese!

00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:54.280
That would be Line.

00:19:54.280 --> 00:19:55.070
Line?

00:19:55.850 --> 00:20:00.230
A liquid drug that's been circulating around these parts for a while.

00:19:58.080 --> 00:20:01.120
Got a problem with me?!

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:03.730
If you use it, your nerves and sensitivity
skyrocket to the point where you're no longer tired.

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:05.020
See ya later.

00:20:03.730 --> 00:20:05.030
Then your body becomes much lighter.

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:10.930
But there's one way Line is
distinctly different from other drugs.

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:16.050
It really amplifies your physical and mental abilities.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:18.980
Does it actually make you stronger?

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:21.040
That's what they say.

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:23.260
It's still a one-time deal kind of thing.

00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:27.120
On the same topic, there's a high demand for it.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:29.250
The withdrawal symptoms are intense.

00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:32.610
The thicker the density, the
stronger the withdrawal effects.

00:20:32.610 --> 00:20:35.450
And if the body doesn't adjust to the effects, it'll hurt even more.

00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:37.840
And if it's really bad, then you go on to the next world.

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:40.790
What a terrible drug.

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:45.370
There's nothing against doping in Igra's rules, but...

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:50.010
Eh, I'll just stop right there.

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:03.130
Come to think of it, you're not going to participate in Igra?

00:21:03.470 --> 00:21:06.400
Eh? Right...

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:09.100
Let's go back. Let's get going.

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:10.800
Alright.

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:12.790
We'll see you around, Motomi.

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:13.650
Sure.

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:15.590
See you again!

00:21:25.210 --> 00:21:26.100
Akira!

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:32.800
I can't let you play this dangerous game by yourself!

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:37.380
So... I'll participate in Igra too.

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:41.820
Don't even try to stop me.

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:50.720
Do whatever you want.

00:21:51.730 --> 00:21:52.940
All right!

00:21:52.940 --> 00:21:55.730
We have to win this and go home together, Akira!

00:22:10.240 --> 00:22:12.770
Looking for the bright lights

00:22:13.940 --> 00:22:16.250
Kibou no Hoshi ga

00:22:13.940 --> 00:22:16.250
The stars of desire

00:22:17.240 --> 00:22:20.700
Kimi wo Tsutsumi Konde

00:22:17.240 --> 00:22:20.700
wrap around you and

00:22:20.930 --> 00:22:23.180
Boku wo Terasu

00:22:20.930 --> 00:22:23.180
make me illuminate onwards

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:36.770
Egao wo Modoreru Hi Made

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:36.770
Till the day that your smile returns,

00:22:38.770 --> 00:22:42.770
Kokoro wo Kasaneteku

00:22:38.770 --> 00:22:42.770
my heart continues to pile up

00:22:45.710 --> 00:22:50.540
Namida no Imi wo Kowashite

00:22:45.710 --> 00:22:50.540
I break the meaning behind my tears

00:22:52.540 --> 00:22:57.110
Tsuyosa ni Kaete yukou

00:22:52.540 --> 00:22:57.110
and I'll keep on changing them into strengths

00:22:59.090 --> 00:23:01.760
Teri Chotto Kujyuu

00:22:59.090 --> 00:23:01.760
Although the sunshine is a bit bitter,

00:23:02.600 --> 00:23:05.220
Boku ga Ikite Iru

00:23:02.600 --> 00:23:05.220
I am going to keep on living

00:23:05.990 --> 00:23:08.660
Kotae Nante Iranai

00:23:05.990 --> 00:23:08.660
I don't need anything like an answer

00:23:09.050 --> 00:23:12.140
Fumidasou!

00:23:09.050 --> 00:23:12.140
Let's keep moving forward!

00:23:12.460 --> 00:23:14.910
Looking for the bright lights

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:18.430
Ima no Boku wa

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:18.430
My current self

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:22.750
Kimi no Senaka no Koshi ni

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:22.750
is riding on your back

00:23:23.060 --> 00:23:25.240
DOA wo Miteru

00:23:23.060 --> 00:23:25.240
looking at the door

00:23:26.290 --> 00:23:28.720
Looking for the shadow light

00:23:29.950 --> 00:23:32.230
Hito no Namida ga

00:23:29.950 --> 00:23:32.230
Until our tears

00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:36.630
Yawarakaku Neru Made

00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:36.630
can sleep soundly,

00:23:36.910 --> 00:23:39.270
Dakishimetai

00:23:36.910 --> 00:23:39.270
I'll want to embrace you

00:23:39.760 --> 00:23:42.160
Sparkle!

00:23:47.220 --> 00:23:49.210
Boku wo Mamoru

00:23:47.220 --> 00:23:49.210
Keep this promise with me

00:23:49.980 --> 00:23:50.840
Erm, you know—

00:23:50.840 --> 00:23:52.190
What is it, Akira?

00:23:52.190 --> 00:23:54.350
How did you get to Toshima, anyway?

00:23:54.920 --> 00:23:57.250
I got lost in my thoughts and
just started chasing after you.

00:23:57.250 --> 00:23:59.080
I came here in a car, you know.

00:23:59.080 --> 00:24:01.650
Huh? Er, well, yeah.

00:24:01.650 --> 00:24:04.150
I just thought of coming to Toshima to look for you.

00:24:04.150 --> 00:24:06.230
Well, I'd believe that.

00:24:06.230 --> 00:24:10.310
I did ask how you were able to come and chase after my tracks like that.

00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:12.050
For crying out loud, enough already.

00:24:12.050 --> 00:24:14.100
I do wonder how you were able to find me.

00:24:14.100 --> 00:24:16.490
It was since I was lost in my thoughts without you, really.

00:24:14.530 --> 00:24:19.160
Episode 3

00:24:16.490 --> 00:24:18.490
You already said that...
